# This repo is a monorepo: apps/web (Next.js, deployed here) + apps/api
# (a stateful FastAPI backend with a local SQLite DB, local file storage,
# and ML models persisted to local disk). Vercel's build now auto-scans
# the whole repo for deployable frameworks and was finding apps/api as a
# FastAPI candidate, failing the build on missing pyproject.toml config.
# The backend can't run correctly on Vercel's ephemeral serverless
# filesystem anyway (writes wouldn't persist between invocations), so it
# is excluded from this deployment entirely and hosted separately. See
# docs/DEPLOYMENT.md.
apps/api/
requirements.txt
requirements-ml.txt
requirements-ml-advanced.txt
requirements-ml-heavy.txt
Dockerfile
docker-compose.yml
run_app.bat
scripts/
tests/
fixtures/
knowledge/
engineering-rules/
database/
data/
uploads/
outputs/
exports/
logs/
